@startuml
title Interaction Service — reaction consistency and resilience
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor User
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Interaction Controller" as API
participant "Create Interaction Use Case" as Create
participant "TargetAvailabilityPort" as TargetPort
participant "Post or Comment Service" as Target
database "Interaction DB" as DB

User -> Gateway : POST /interaction/api/v1/interactions\nLIKE
Gateway -> API : trusted actor + correlation ID
API -> Create : command(actor, targetType, targetId, reactionType)
Create -> TargetPort : ensureAvailable(...)
TargetPort -> Target : Feign availability check

alt Target missing/deleted
  Target --> TargetPort : 404 or available=false
  TargetPort --> Create : TargetNotFound
  Create --> API : no ledger/counter write
  API --> Gateway : 404
  Gateway --> User : target-not-found response
else Dependency timeout/5xx
  TargetPort -> Target : one bounded retry
  TargetPort --> Create : DependencyUnavailable
  Create --> API : fail closed
  API --> Gateway : 503
  Gateway --> User : dependency-unavailable response
else Target available
  Target --> TargetPort : available
  group One local database transaction
    Create -> DB : INSERT ledger ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
    alt Row inserted
      Create -> DB : upsert counter row + atomic increment
      DB --> Create : created=true
    else Same reaction already exists
      DB --> Create : created=false, duplicateIgnored=true
    end
    Create -> DB : read authoritative ledger row
  end
  Create --> API : current reaction state
  API --> Gateway : 200
  Gateway --> User : reaction response
end

note over Create,DB
  ADR-002: one reaction per actor and target.
  V1 supports LIKE only; unique key excludes reactionType.
end note

== Remove is local and idempotent ==
User -> Gateway : DELETE /interaction/api/v1/interactions/{type}/{id}/{reaction}
Gateway -> API : trusted actor
API -> DB : atomic delete ledger row
alt Row removed
  API -> DB : guarded counter decrement in same transaction
  API --> Gateway : 200, data=true
  Gateway --> User : removed
else Already absent
  API --> Gateway : 200, data=false; counter unchanged
  Gateway --> User : already absent
end

== Reads do not depend on target providers ==
User -> Gateway : GET actor reactions / counters
Gateway -> API : request
API -> DB : local query (single or batch)
DB --> API : ledger/counters; missing counter = zero
API --> Gateway : 200 even if Post/Comment is down
Gateway --> User : local read response
@enduml
